"## Flow: 816\n\n- **Platform**: web\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/flows/816\n- **Name**: Employee report creation\n- **Screens Count**: 5\n- **Description**: Happy-path: A signed-in user navigates to the Analytics > Reports section, adds a new employee report via the Employees panel, names the report in a modal, creates it, inspects the populated report table, then returns to the Reports list where the new report appears. Entry: Analytics > Reports tab. Exit: Reports list showing the newly created employee report. Assumptions: User is authenticated and has permission to view Analytics and create reports; using desktop browser (wide layout) because of visible three-column layout and modal.\n- **Problem**: Task: Create and view an employee report from the Analytics Reports area. From the user's perspective: they want to add a new employee report, give it a clear name, inspect the generated employee data (columns and rows), and confirm the report is saved and accessible later. Key decisions: choose where to add the report (Employees section), supply a descriptive name, review or refine the generated table. From the interface/system perspective: the Reports list exposes categories (Time-off, Employees, Devices, Audits) each with a plus control to add a new report; clicking the Employees + opens a modal that requires a Name; creating the report opens the report editor/table populated with employee fields; saving/closing returns the user to the Reports list where the new report is enumerated with metadata (e.g., scheduled email status). End result: user-perceived outcome — a named employee report is created and visible in the Reports list and its data can be inspected and exported; system-level outcome — a new report object is created and persisted (no schedule assigned by default), accessible in the Employees reports collection.\n\n### Site\n- **ID**: 545\n- **Name**: Aboard\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/websites/545\n- **Domain**: aboardhr.com\n- **Categories**: Paperwork, Collaboration Tools\n- **Description**: Joyful HR\n\n### Steps\n\n#### Step 1: Reports listing — Employees panel\n- **Screen ID**: c189ea3e-5ead-4cc8-9df8-82acaedcd015\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/pages/c189ea3e-5ead-4cc8-9df8-82acaedcd015\n- **ThumbnailURL**: https://images.refero.design/screenshots/aboardhr.com/desktop/21c90ea3-dfcd-4713-89f3-d31b7f8a7b7b_thumb.jpg\n- **Goal**: Start creating a new employee report from the Analytics > Reports area.\n- **Action**: Click the plus (+) control in the Employees section (or the floating plus inside the Employees area).\n- **System Response**: UI highlights the Employees add interaction and opens a 'New employee report' modal centered over the Reports screen.\n- **UI Elements**: Tooltip\n- **Fonts**: Intercom, Inter\n- **Content**\n  - Description: An analytics dashboard for Refero Design with a warm beige theme, a left navigation sidebar, and a main overview panel showing report categories for Time-off, Employees, Devices, and Audits.\n  - Layout: Two-column layout with a narrow left sidebar menu and a wide main content area; the main area has a top header, Overview/Reports tabs, and four stacked card-like report sections.\n  - Functions: Lets users navigate organization tools from the sidebar, switch between overview and reports, view summary report categories, and use plus/ellipsis controls for adding or managing report entries.\n\n#### Step 2: New employee report modal (empty)\n- **Screen ID**: 612c4cc3-cef1-4f48-b37b-1d7abfdb132b\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/pages/612c4cc3-cef1-4f48-b37b-1d7abfdb132b\n- **ThumbnailURL**: https://images.refero.design/screenshots/aboardhr.com/desktop/2c399a35-c0c3-4dad-8d94-7fa75028dc08_thumb.jpg\n- **Goal**: Provide a name for the new employee report.\n- **Action**: Type a descriptive name into the Name input field. Options available: Cancel or Create.\n- **System Response**: The modal accepts input; the Create button becomes the primary action to submit the form (Cancel closes the modal without changes).\n- **UX Patterns**: Add & Create\n- **UI Elements**: Button, Text Field, Dialog & Modal Window\n- **Fonts**: Intercom, Inter\n- **Content**\n  - Description: An analytics dashboard for Refero Design with a left navigation sidebar, an Analytics page showing Overview/Reports tabs, report sections like Time-off, Employee, Devices, and Audits, and a centered modal titled \"New employee report\" with a name input and Cancel/Create buttons.\n  - Layout: Two-column layout with a left sidebar and main content area; the main area has a top tab bar, stacked report sections below, and a centered modal overlay with a simple form and action buttons.\n  - Functions: Lets users navigate dashboard sections, view analytics report categories, and create a new employee report by entering a name in the modal and choosing Cancel or Create.\n\n#### Step 3: New employee report modal (filled)\n- **Screen ID**: 8147eb17-2ab4-41d2-a5db-525a582a0e2e\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/pages/8147eb17-2ab4-41d2-a5db-525a582a0e2e\n- **ThumbnailURL**: https://images.refero.design/screenshots/aboardhr.com/desktop/738a1793-ab60-4a48-9dea-7fbc5a008021_thumb.jpg\n- **Goal**: Confirm the report name and submit creation.\n- **Action**: Click Create to finalize the report name and generate the report.\n- **System Response**: Modal submits and the interface navigates to the newly created report's editor/viewer.\n- **UX Patterns**: Add & Create\n- **UI Elements**: Button, Text Field, Dialog & Modal Window\n- **Fonts**: Intercom, Inter\n- **Content**\n  - Description: A corporate analytics dashboard for “Refero Design” in a muted beige/gray/blue theme, showing a left navigation sidebar, an Overview/Reports tab bar, stacked report categories, and a centered modal for creating a new employee report.\n  - Layout: Two-column layout with a fixed left sidebar and a fluid main content area; the main area has top tabs, vertically stacked report sections with plus icons, and a centered overlay modal with a title, input field, and action buttons.\n  - Functions: Lets users navigate analytics sections, view grouped report categories and scheduled reports, and create a new report through the modal using the text field plus Cancel or Create actions.\n\n#### Step 4: Report editor — table view\n- **Screen ID**: dd8cd46c-9f42-487f-9027-5f8985afda33\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/pages/dd8cd46c-9f42-487f-9027-5f8985afda33\n- **ThumbnailURL**: https://images.refero.design/screenshots/aboardhr.com/desktop/99bb3452-a7cc-4698-82f3-6ae4974dad3f_thumb.jpg\n- **Goal**: Review the content of the newly created employee report.\n- **Action**: Inspect the populated table (columns like Full name, Job title, Daily/Weekly working hours, Workdays), optionally add filters, export, or Save changes.\n- **System Response**: Report editor displays employee rows and columns; controls for adding filters, exporting, and saving are available. Changes can be saved or the user can navigate back to the Reports list.\n- **UX Patterns**: Add & Create\n- **UI Elements**: Table, Button, Dropdown, Sidebar & Drawer, Icon, Avatar\n- **Fonts**: Intercom, Inter\n- **Content**\n  - Description: Clean business analytics screen showing a monthly employee report with a pale left navigation sidebar, a beige top header with a trial-mode badge, and a large employee hours table in the main area.\n  - Layout: Two-column layout with a full-height left sidebar and a right content panel containing a header toolbar above a wide, horizontally aligned data table.\n  - Functions: Lets users review employee work-hour data, filter the report, switch table views, download/export data, and save changes while navigating other app sections from the sidebar.\n\n#### Step 5: Reports listing — new report visible\n- **Screen ID**: 23a4cf44-30e1-4879-9cc3-f08b6bb21f2c\n- **ReferoURL**: https://refero.design/pages/23a4cf44-30e1-4879-9cc3-f08b6bb21f2c\n- **ThumbnailURL**: https://images.refero.design/screenshots/aboardhr.com/desktop/ca91de02-b952-4f74-916d-3dfc5432a151_thumb.jpg\n- **Goal**: Confirm the report was created and is listed under Employees.\n- **Action**: Observe the Employees section where 'Monthly employee report' (or the chosen name) appears with metadata (e.g., 'No scheduled email'), and use kebab menu for additional actions.\n- **System Response**: Reports list shows the new employee report item; system has persisted the report and displays its status. The report can be opened again from this list.\n- **Page Types**: Content Management Page\n- **UI Elements**: List, Button, Tabs, Sidebar & Drawer, Icon\n- **Fonts**: Intercom, Inter\n- **Content**\n  - Description: Clean corporate analytics dashboard with a light beige sidebar, white main panel, and a yellow trial-mode banner. It shows grouped report cards for Time-off, Employees, Devices, and Audits with minimal icon-based controls.\n  - Layout: Two-column desktop layout with a vertical left navigation sidebar and a main content area on the right. The main area has a header, Overview/Reports tabs, and four stacked analytics cards with add and overflow controls.\n  - Functions: Supports navigation through the sidebar, switching between Overview and Reports tabs, viewing report statuses, and adding/configuring reports via plus buttons and overflow menus. Also shows trial remaining time and empty states for unavailable reports.\n\n### Related Queries\n- analytics reports management\n- create new employee report\n- reports list add report\n- employee report modal name\n- open report table view\n- monthly employee data table\n- save and export report\n- report listed under employees\n- add filter to report\n- report scheduling indicator"
